<description>
Recolor the two sprite masks whose pixelwise union equals a third sprite mask.

Input structure
- The grid has black background and red foreground arranged as six 4x4
  sprite regions in a 3-by-2 array, separated by blank rows and columns.
- Each sprite region contains a non-empty red mask.
- Exactly one sprite is the pixelwise OR of two other sprite masks, except
  that duplicate operand copies are resolved by row-major position.

Rule
- Find two operand sprites whose foreground masks each contribute at least
  one unique pixel and whose union exactly matches a destination sprite.
- Recolor the operand sprite pixels teal and recolor the destination sprite
  pixels green; leave all other pixels unchanged.

Key insight
- The three changed sprites are identified by a mask-union relation; position
  matters only when identical operand copies create the same relation.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_to_match",
  "src": "red 4x4 sprite masks s in the 3-by-2 array",
  "dst": "red sprite mask d in the same array",
  "match_cond": "two distinct s masks have pixelwise union equal to d, and each contributes at least one pixel",
  "transform": "recolor the two matched operand sprites teal and d green; leave all other pixels unchanged",
  "multi_step": "if duplicate operand copies make the same relation, use the row-major earliest copy"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: fixed 16x11, black background
  layout: 3x2 array of 4x4 sprite cells, 1-cell gaps and margins on all sides
  sprites:
    count: 6 (always)
    color: all red (color 2) in input
    cell_size: 4x4
    pixels_per_sprite: 7-14 (holes = 2-9 per 4x4 cell)
    each_sprite: non-empty (>=1 pixel)
    connectivity: 1-3 components per sprite [observed]
  union_relation:
    exactly one destination sprite d whose mask = mask_a | mask_b for two operand sprites a, b
    each operand contributes >=1 unique pixel (a has pixel not in b, and vice versa)
    operand overlap: 4-12 pixels
    if duplicate operand copies create ambiguous triples, all share the same destination
  distractors: remaining 3 sprites must NOT form any additional union triple with a different destination
  output:
    same grid, same layout
    operand sprites a,b recolored teal (color 8)
    destination sprite d recolored green (color 3)
    other 3 sprites remain red
    no structural changes, only color substitution

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Create two random non-empty 4x4 binary masks (operands a, b) such that each has >=1 unique pixel and their union is non-trivial (not identical to either operand).
    2. Compute destination mask d = a | b.
    3. Generate 3 distractor 4x4 masks randomly. Validate that no pair of {a, b, d0, d1, d2} unions to any other member (or if so, only with same destination d). Reject and retry if violated.
    4. Shuffle all 6 sprites into a random permutation across the 3x2 grid positions.
    5. Build 16x11 grid: 1-row/col black margins, 1-row/col black gaps between cells. Place all masks as red pixels.
```
</generation_spec>
